== verdict
==============================================================================
  TRIPLET T1 above 0.04 at r = 2.20, 2.40, 2.60 A
  This is the surface the wavepacket moves on, so this is the
  one that matters. If the flagged points are a contiguous
  region rather than scattered, the state-specific route needs
  a multireference patch there -- or the whole triplet surface
  needs CASSCF/NEVPT2 after all.

  Singlet T1 above 0.02 from r = 2.60 A outward. EXPECTED: the ground state becomes
  a diradical that RHF cannot represent. Harmless, provided the
  ground-state surface is built only over the bound region, as
  water/13_gs_well.py does. Treat min(flagged r) as the outer
  limit of where V_gs may be trusted.

  cost: 11620 CPU-s for 14 points = 830 CPU-s/point (364 s wall)
  a 3289-point raster at this rate: 758 CPU-hours = 47 h on 16 cores
